nss-rk.qos is an SQM script for Qualcomm NSS hardware offload (nsstbl +
nssfq_codel) with port based traffic classes (nftables marks + DSCP).

Select the queue discipline "fq_codel" and this script. Only fq_codel is
supported. Only ONE SQM instance is supported (shared nssifb / nft table).

Only the low byte (0xff) of the packet/conntrack mark is used; other mark bits
are preserved.

Options in /etc/config/trafficchart (section global) or LuCI "Traffic Chart Settings";
the extras are OFF by default:
  option dns_redirect '1'            redirect DNS from all non-WAN interfaces
  option dns_redirect_exclude 'wg0'  interfaces left out of that redirect
  option ttl_fix '1'                 rewrite TTL / hop limit 63,127 -> 64
  option reset_ct_marks '0'          keep the ct marks on (re)start (default 1 = zero them
                                     so every flow is classified again; use 0 with mwan3)

Restart SQM after changing any of them.

Script options (SQM "Advanced" page):
  ETARGET / ITARGET     codel target (default 5ms)
  ELIMIT / ILIMIT       queue limit in packets (default: calculated, 100 ms)
  EQDISC_OPTS / IQDISC_OPTS   extra nssfq_codel options (interval, quantum, flows)
